{"authoredAt":"2026-08-20T17:09:48.852Z","conclusion":"findings","findings":[{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-promise-undelivered: docs/host-run-usage.md:109-127 promises that asynchronous late EPIPE remains contained until it fires, but packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts:500-507 releases the shared guard from the write callback. Node Writable invokes that callback before emitting the corresponding 'error'; a delayed real Writable reproduced write-callback followed by uncaught late-EPIPE after host_run returned. packages/main/src/tasks/host-run-usage-smoke.ts:2216-2261 only invokes fake callbacks and never emits the post-callback error, so it misses the real ordering. A completed foreground host_run can therefore crash the CLI instead of surfacing passthroughError. Retain containment through the post-callback error turn and add a real Writable regression.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/tasks/host-run-usage-smoke.ts"],"severity":"critical"},{"category":"adversarial","desc":"quality-correctness: packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts:1629-1651 captures exitCode before asynchronous process-group cleanup but leaves startup/total timers armed until finish() at line 1391. If a deadline fires during the up-to-500ms TERM/KILL cleanup window, terminate() changes timedOut, timeoutKind, and terminalReason after exitCode is fixed. A deterministic fake-runtime run returned exitCode=0, timedOut=true, timeoutKind=total_timeout, terminalReason=total_timeout, replacementSafe=true; packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:971-982 then persists and digest-binds that contradictory result. Fence or cancel timers when close wins, or compute exitCode after cleanup from the winning terminal state, and cover the close-versus-deadline race.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts","packages/main/src/tasks/host-run-usage-sm